## Finding Index (first pass, one line per finding)

### CORS (12) — CRITICAL 9.1
- CORS Wildcard/Arbitrary Origin with Credentials — MikuNime_MITM & variants
  - `curl -I -H 'Origin: https://evil.com' https://adservice.google.com/getconfig/pubvendors`
  - Any authenticated endpoint reflecting arbitrary Origin → cross-origin data theft

### CodeExecution (1) — CRITICAL 8.1
- Application Is Debuggable — vionime
  - `jdb -connect com.sun.jdi.SocketAttach:hostname=localhost,port=8700`
  - Debuggable flag allows JDI attach → arbitrary method invocation in app context

### NetworkSecurity (20) — HIGH 7.5
- Network Security Config Trusts User Certificates — MikuNime_0.3.2 & variants
  - `res/xml/network_security_config.xml` includes `<certificates src="user"/>` and cleartext permitted
  - Combined with MITM: full plaintext TLS interception of app traffic
- (repeat across all MikuNime merged/FINAL/NOPAIRIP patched+unsigned variants)

### ComponentAbuse (30) — HIGH 7.2
- Unprotected Exported Activity: com.google.firebase.auth.internal.GenericIdpActivity — MikuNime_0.3.2
  - `adb shell am start -n com.mikunime.app.id/com.google.firebase.auth.internal.GenericIdpActivity`
  - Exported Firebase IDP activity → phishing / token interception attack surface
- Exported components across MikuNime + Vionime + ManhwaID variants (provider/activity/service/receiver)

### DataExposure (6) — MEDIUM 5.5
- Application Data Backup Allowed — split_config.arm64_v8a (ManhwaID)
  - `adb backup -f backup.ab -noapk com.ghavadev.mangaindo`
  - `android:allowBackup="true"` (default) → full app-private data extraction via backup stream
- Shared prefs / internal DB exposure across other splits

### AuthN/AuthZ (1) — HIGH 7.5, Anibi Play
- IDOR — User Profile Dump
  - `curl -s https://api.kisame.cloud/api/v2/user/profile/1 -H 'Authorization: Bearer <JWT>'`
  - Enumeratable user profile IDs with a valid JWT → mass profile exposure

### MissingAuthN (1) — HIGH 8.1, Anibi Play
- Payment Gateway — No Authentication
  - `curl -s 'https://pakasir.anibi.cloud/api/user?email=<target_email>'`
  - Unauthenticated payment-gateway user lookup → email enumeration / payment data exposure

### RateLimit (1) — MEDIUM 5.3, Anibi Play
- No Rate Limiting
  - `ab -n 500 -c 50 https://api.kisame.cloud/api/v2/user/profile/1`
  - Enables brute force / bulk enumeration against authenticated endpoints

### WebSocket (1) — MEDIUM 6.5, Anibi Play
- WebSocket Unauthorized Access
  - `curl -s 'https://api.kisame.cloud/chat/socket.io/?EIO=4&transport=polling'`
  - socket.io handshake completes without auth → chat/P2P data exposure

